     A*
     A* The ICF file the application sends an order over: a record it
     A* writes to the remote program, one it reads back, and the
     A* responses the communications support returns in the indicators.
     A*
     A* Member: ORDICF   Compilable: yes (CRTICFF)
     A* Source: DDS for ICF files, IBM i 7.5.
     A* Retrieved: 2026-07-28
     A*
     A*
     A* File level: the indicator area, and the keyword that sends
     A* the record format name to the remote program on output.
     A* FMTNAME takes no parameters.
     A                                      INDARA
     A                                      FMTNAME
     A*
     A* The record sent to the remote program. EVOKE starts it and
     A* the invite lets the program read from it later.
     A          R ORDOUT                    EVOKE(&LIB/&PGM)
     A                                      SECURITY(1 &USR 2 &PWD)
     A                                      SYNLVL(*CONFIRM)
     A                                      INVITE
     A* Data fields carry B or a blank usage. The reference allows
     A* no other value: I and O belong to display and printer files.
     A            ORDNBR         7P 0B
     A            ORDAMT        11P 2
     A*
     A* Program-to-system fields carry P and must be defined after
     A* every data field. They supply the values the keywords name.
     A            LIB           10A  P
     A            PGM           10A  P
     A            USR           10A  P
     A            PWD           10A  P
     A*
     A* The record read back, and the responses the support sets.
     A          R ORDIN                     RCVENDGRP(21)
     A                                      RCVCONFIRM(22)
     A                                      RCVDETACH(23)
     A                                      RCVFAIL(24)
     A                                      RCVTRNRND(25)
     A                                      TIMER
     A            RSPCOD         2A  B
     A            RSPTXT        50A
     A*
     A* Control operations, each on a record of its own.
     A          R ORDCNF                    CONFIRM
     A          R ORDDTC                    DETACH
     A          R ORDFAI                    FAIL
     A          R ORDNEG                    NEGRSP
     A          R ORDRQW                    RQSWRT
     A          R ORDEOG                    ENDGRP
